{
  "abstract": "We give explicit rank-zero elliptic images of genus-two intermediate quotients arising from two components of the regular-quintuple path stratum. For the previously excluded component $C_{13}$, degree-three maps prove a decomposition of its genus-two Jacobian into elliptic factors, replace the genus-two descent and Chabauty computation by an elementary seven-point calculation, and explain the annihilating differential algebraically. For $C_{14}$, previously known only numerically, we certify the degree-22 entry model and identify a genus-two quotient whose second involution gives a rank-zero elliptic image. Its ten rational points, combined with an exceptional-fiber argument, exclude every rational point of the affine entry image with distinct nonzero coordinates. The lifting argument covers singular-image points without assuming a rational lift to the normalization. The two applications distinguish the finite elliptic image from an invariant quotient with positive rank and do not rely on a complete component census. The rational Diophantine septuple problem remains open.",
